<BaseLayout title="Reliable ML begins before the model | The Hidden Lemma"><article class="prose"><p class="meta"><a href="/notes/">notes</a> / machine learning · 12 September 2026</p><h1>Reliable ML begins before the model</h1><p>A model can perform well in a notebook and still fail in production. Often the failure starts upstream, where data changes quietly and assumptions remain undocumented.</p><h2>Start with contracts</h2><p>Define expected fields, ranges, freshness, ownership, and failure behaviour. A contract makes assumptions observable and testable.</p><h2>Make the path visible</h2><p>Track lineage from source to feature to prediction. Version data, code, configuration, and artifacts together.</p><h2>Monitor the whole system</h2><p>Latency, missingness, drift, cost, and feedback quality are part of model performance.</p></article></BaseLayout>
